Files: usr/share/sparky/sparky-stereo-hardware/network-ids.tsv, usr/lib/sparky-stereo-hardware/detect.py (the Broadcom device list, the CPU level test)
    Values and methods taken from other projects, named in the comments of those files:
    - CachyOS (https://github.com/CachyOS), chwd profile broadcom-wl (GPL-3.0): the Broadcom device list; cachyos-repo.sh: the test of the loader's "(supported, searched)" lines for the CPU level. Read 2026-10-05.
    - Debian, broadcom-sta-dkms README: the Broadcom IDs the closed wl driver supports. Read 2026-10-05.
    - The Linux kernel (GPL-2.0-only): the ID tables and modules.alias of the MediaTek and Realtek drivers.
    - The OpenRGB project (https://openrgb.org), udev rules documentation: the USB vendors named as RGB makers.
    - apt (GPL-2.0+), test/integration/varianttable: the CPU flags of each x86-64 level.
    License: as the projects state; our packaging of them GPL-3+

